        },
        {
          "label": "D",
          "html": "80°"
        }
      ],
      "figures": [
        "szkolny_2017-2018_malopolskie_q5_fig1.png"
      ],
      "answer": {
        "correct": "C",
        "solution_html": null,
        "model": {
          "answer": "D",
          "by": "sonnet",
          "agrees": false,
          "solution_html": "<p>The three lines form a triangle. The shaded 60° at the top is vertical to the triangle's interior angle there, so that interior angle = 60°.</p><p>The shaded 140° is the exterior angle at the bottom-right vertex, adjacent (supplementary) to the interior angle there, so interior angle = 180−140 = 40°.</p><p>By the exterior-angle theorem (or angle sum 180°): α = 180−60−40 = 80°.</p>"
        }
      }
